To achieve this in PHP, you can use the ImageMagick extension to convert JPEG/PNG files into PSD format and set the correct MIME type for Photoshop:

```php
$image = new Imagick();
$image->readImage("myImage.jpg");
$image->setImageFormat('psd');
header('Content-type: image/photoshop'); 
die($image);
```

This code reads a JPEG file, converts it to PSD format using ImageMagick, and sets the MIME type for Photoshop. The browser will then open the PSD file with Photoshop if installed.

For opening PSD files in Illustrator, you can use:

```app.preferences.photoshopFileOptions.preserveHiddenLayers = true;```

This line of code is part of a larger script that opens PSD files in Illustrator and applies settings like preserving hidden layers.

