dense_raw_answer:
To solve your issue, you can use absolute positioning for both the background div and content divs within it. This way, only the background image fades out while keeping other elements visible:

```html
<div id="hpbg-image">
    <div id="stuff">
        <div id="header">...</div>
        <div id="search-area">...</div>
        <div id="content1" style="height:150px">No minimum contract, pay for everything online</div>
        <div id="howitworks"><b>How it works</b></div>
        <div id="freelancers" style="height:300px"></div>
    </div>
</div>

#hpbg-image {
    position:absolute;
}

#stuff {
    position:absolute;
}
```

This ensures the content remains visible while only the background image fades out.

